C++ AGG 2.6 image and pattern filter fixes that agg-rust carries: every RGB/RGBA span image
filter and pattern_filter_bilinear_rgba starts its weighted sums at half a unit (C++ starts most
at 0 and truncates, darkening by half a level on average), the resamplers add half the total
weight before dividing, and span_image_resample_rgba clamps colour to alpha (C++ compares each
channel with itself). Apply from the repo root to render the patched C++ references:
  patch -p0 < tools/cpp-renderer/patches/agg_image_filter-rounding-fixes.patch
then revert with patch -R -p0 so cpp-references stays pristine.

